        "original_id": "0e9fdfdc-e2dc-5c4e-a115-5cc39810d378",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Saipan, Battle of Manila (1945)\n- Places: Saipan, Mariana Islands, Manila, Philippines\n- Organizations: U.S. 2nd Marine Division, 4th Marine Division, 27th Infantry Division, Imperial Japanese Army\n- People: Holland Smith, Yoshitsugu Saito\n- Topics: Pacific campaign of World War II\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Saipan was a battle in the Pacific campaign of World War II fought on Saipan in the Mariana Islands from 15 June 1944 to 9 July 1944.\n- In the Battle of Saipan, the U.S. 2nd Marine Division, 4th Marine Division, and Army 27th Infantry Division were commanded by Lieutenant General Holland Smith.\n- In the Battle of Saipan, the U.S. forces defeated the 43rd Infantry Division of the Imperial Japanese Army, which was commanded by Lieutenant General Yoshitsugu Saito.\n- The Battle of Manila (1945) was fought in Manila, the capital of the Philippines, by American and Filipino forces against Japanese troops.",
